// A function crossing an argument edge carries its PARAMETERS' refinements
// the other way: the lambda hands its argument to `alpha`, so it demands an
// `Hz` of every value it is called with, and `drive` calls it with
// `sweep(t)` — a Float nothing proves is below the ceiling (sweep(1.0) is
// 70,900). Those values live inside `drive`'s body, not at this edge, so the
// claim cannot be decided here: the compile SURFACES it as V_Pending debt
// and runs. On boot 43aeb30f the predicate was dropped at the unification,
// with no debt and no refusal — the Pulse renderer's filter took a 70,900 Hz
// sweep and checked clean. Reaching the values inside the callee is
// `Hβ.verify.higher-order-refinement`'s refinement variables.

type Hz = Float where 0.0 < self && self < 22050.0

fn alpha(c: Hz) -> Float = c * 2.0

fn sweep(t: Float) -> Float = 900.0 + 70000.0 * t

fn drive(f, t: Float) = f(sweep(t))

fn main() = if drive((c) => alpha(c), 1.0) > 0.0 { 0 } else { 1 }
